Subject: [PATCH 09857/11362] [outer-loop] Full-suite: root cause is the
 janitor, not a hang

Second baseline attempt captured the exit code outside the owning shell:
EXIT_CODE=137 (SIGKILL), wall 7386s, END 2026-08-24T22:55:51Z.
/tmp/orphan-cleanup.log records "22:55:50Z killed 1 orphan workers".
One second apart.

~/.carnot/orphan-cleanup.sh kill -9's any process whose comm is python3 or
pytest past THRESHOLD_MIN=120 unless it descends from the conductor; the
timer fires every 30min. The serial suite needs >2h. So a serial full-suite
run cannot complete on this box and never could. Not a deadlock, not a
product failure -- infrastructure killing the measurement.

setsid, used to survive the agent harness, is what made the run an orphan.
Hardening against one killer handed it to another.

Both runs stopped at the same index (11905 vs 11910 tests, 74F/9s both) at
1487s and 7386s -- ordering is deterministic and the 74 failures in the
first 20% are reproducible. The death index is NOT a poison test: those
19 tests in isolation give 1 failed / 18 passed in 33s, exit 1.

Recommendation zero added: make the run fit the window (-n 4 --no-cov),
or give the janitor a marked-run exemption. Explicitly rejects evading the
comm match, while noting the matcher is narrower than its concept.

